'''Mastery''' is a set of challenges for each [[Toon]]. The reward for completion is the Toon's {{Skin|Vintage}} [[Skin]], and Mastery on certain Toons is a requirement to purchase other ones (as of {{GameVersion}}). The loading menu suggests that additional lore will be unlocked through Mastery in future updates.

==Uses==
Uses for Mastery are:
*Obtaining the Toon's Vintage [[Skin]]
*Prerequisite to buy a [[Toon]]

==Description==
Each [[Toon]] comes with 6 quests to accomplish known as "Mastery quests". The tasks can be things like traveling a certain distance, surviving a number of [[Floors]], or finishing a number of [[Machines]]. The quests are usually catered to the Toon's specific strengths and [[Abilities]]. Completing all 6 Mastery quests on a Toon grants their Vintage [[Skin]]. All Vintage Skins change the Toon's color palette to monochrome and add highlight slits to their eyes (similar to old cartoons). However, the Vintage Skins are not a 1:1 grayscale version of their normal colors and often modify their brightness; if the Toon was already black and white (such as {{CI|Blot|name=true}}), most or all colors will change shades. Once Mastery is obtained, the Toon will gain two small, yellow sparkles on the top-right corner of their icon in the Toons menu. Mastery quests for any particular Toon only gain progress while that specific Toon is being used.

Certain Toons require you to complete or partially complete Mastery on another Toon before you can purchase them. For example, you must fully master {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} to be able to purchase {{CI|Vee|name=true}}. This means you must complete all 6 quests for Brightney (which requires purchasing her) to fulfill that unlock requirement.

You can see your Mastery by going to 'Toons' (in the [[Lobby]]) then clicking on the Toon, then clicking on 'Mastery' or clicking 'Stats' in a run. Alternatively, you can also check your Mastery by checking the Mastery TV inside the [[Elevator]] during a run. Once you have completed the Mastery, you must click 'CLAIM' (a green button underneath the Toon's Mastery) to claim their Vintage Skin. 

Mastery is frequently onerous to acquire on a {{Type|Main}}.

