==Strategies==
This will give you tips to complete the most frequent Mastery quests that usually show up for a Toon. For more detailed tips on how to complete a specific quest for a specific Toon, go to their own articles instead.
===Item Usage/Obtainment===
*For this quest, it's recommended to use [[Trinkets]] that grant you Items early on {{TI|Crayon Set|name=true}}, {{TI|Megaphone|name=true}} and {{TI|Pop Pack|name=true}}.
*It's also a good idea to have a [[Toon]] joining you that can help you by generating more Items like {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} or {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, or a Toon that can help you find Items quicker like {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Coal|name=true}}, or {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}.
*Prioritize {{II|Gumballs|name=false}} and {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false}} for the use x Items quests, since they will provide more uses for an Item due to being multi-use.
*Note buying Items from [[Dandy's Shop]] counts as picking up an Item, so Tape gaining Trinkets like {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}} can be viable.
*You can also use the {{SI|Over here!|name=true}} Sticker to alert other players of Items and {{SI|Candy here!|name=true}} for specifically candy Items, and the {{SI|Bandage here!|name=true}} and {{SI|Medkit here!|name=true}} Stickers for healing Items. You can also use the {{SI|Golden Brick|name=true}} or {{SI|Golden Sprout!|name=true}} Sticker as they are seen by everyone and can make traversal easier.

===Meters Travelled===
*It is advised to equip speed [[Trinkets]] (recommended {{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}} and another Trinket like {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}, {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}, or {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}), and move around the first [[Floor]] as much as possible without leaving the Floor.
*If the [[Toon]] you need to complete this quest has 3+ {{Star}} [[Movement Speed]], you can also try to distract for your team to make it less boring.
*If the Toon is slow, you could use {{TI|Cooler|name=true}} with Clown Horn to sprint for longer without losing a lot of speed.
*Find [[Items]] like {{II|Speed Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Eject Button|name=false}}, and {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false}} to move faster and a {{II|Stamina Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Protein Bar|name=false}}, {{II|Pop|name=false}}, and {{II|Bottle o' Pop|name=false}} to sprint for longer.
*You can invite {{CI|Astro|name=true}} to help refill your Stamina so you can sprint for longer, {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} & {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} to help you move faster, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} & {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} to drop speed-related Items, {{CI|Bobette|name=true}} for her Stamina and speed-enhancing Passive Ability, and {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} to speed you up for a few seconds when the Elevator opens.
*During the [[Iced Over]] or [[Spring Fever]] Floor Events, it also greatly helps with the Mastery as it grants every Toons a speed boost as well, though be careful of the challenge that these events also bring up.

===Active Ability Usage===
*Just equip both {{TI|Ghost Snakes In A Can|name=true}} and {{TI|Sweet Charm|name=true}} and try to use your [[Ability]] as much as possible.
*Voting on {{CDI|Rehearsal/Practice|name=true}} can also help to reduce the Toon's Active Ability cooldown.
*You can have a {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} consistently place his trail to remove a chunk of your cooldown, though you’ll have to make sure to stand in it until the flames disappear in order to get the most of the 2x countdown speed.
*If the [[Toon]] you need to complete this Mastery quest is a healer Toon, try to invite someone in a duo run and ask them to take as many hits as possible. {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} and {{CI|Looey|name=true}} are more recommended for this as they have a quest to activate their Passive Abilities, which requires them to lose a {{Heart}}.
**If you need it on {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}, then another strategy is to ask another Cosmo to join a duo run and have one of you intentionally take a hit. After that, just keep healing each other back and forth until you (both) have the quest progress done.
**You can also invite a {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} so when she gets hit, you can take the candies and finish your Item Masteries.
*If the Toon needs {{Tape|name=true}} to use their Ability, swap one of the Trinkets out for {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}} and, if you run out of Tapes, restart and do a new run.
**You can also ask a {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} to give you {{II|BonBon|name=true}}s for more Tape income.
*Keep in mind that {{CI|Bassie|name=true}} has no cooldown for her Active Ability, so you can easily complete this quest by finding a safe spot and spam drop/pick up an Item repeatedly.

===Floors Reached/Survived===
*Just try to find a good team to go to the highest [[Floor]] as you can faster.
*If you want, you can use {{TI|Savory Charm|name=true}} to save yourself from a fatal attack if you tend to die early on. Keep in mind this is a '''one-time use''' and will not save you from a {{Type|Lethal}} attack.
*Vote on {{CDI|First Aid/Medical Attention|name=true}} when on low Health to survive longer.
*Leave {{Tape|name=true}} for {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} so they can use their Active [[Ability]], or Bassie so she can buy more Items from Dandy's Shop for you and your teammates, and prioritize healing Items for healer Toons like {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} so he can heal you and your teammates in situations where you are low on Health.

===Blackout Experience===
*Similar to the quest above, as higher [[Floors]] increase [[Blackout]] chances, and try not to vote on the {{CDI|Electrician|name=true}} Card. Instead, vote for {{CDI|Piping Tape|name=true}} as soon as it shows up to maximize the Blackout probability.
*Try to progress on this when no other events like [[Easter Event]] or [[Christmas Event]] are active, as their exclusive Floor Events, [[Spring Fever]] and [[Iced Over]], can further reduce the probability of Blackouts to occur when they are chosen to be picked instead.
*It's also easier to progress on this one if {{CI|Twisted Brightney|name=true}} occupies the [[Daily Twisted Board]], since her appearance can increase the chance of Blackouts occurring on the Floors she resides in.

===Twisted Encounters===
*Similar to survive x [[Floors]], just try to encounter as many [[Twisteds]] as you can as you go through each Floor.
*If you are in a run and a distractor is present, it is recommended to wait in the [[Elevator]] during [[Panic Mode]], ask the distractor to bring the Twisteds, and step out when the distractor is about to go in.

===[[Machine]] Completion===
*It's recommended to use [[Extraction Speed]] or [[Skill Check]] [[Trinkets]] for this, like {{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}, {{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}, {{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}, etc. to extract Machines much faster.
*You can also have another [[Toon]] to prime the Machines and complete them yourself.
*Vote on {{CDI|Tech Savvy|name=true}} whenever you get a chance to speed up the quest progression even more.
*Invite Toons like {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} or {{CI|Brusha|name=true}} to be able to extract faster.
*Use [[Items]] like a {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false}}, a {{II|BonBon|name=false}}, {{II|Instructions|name=false}}, or an {{II|Extraction Speed Candy|name=false}} to make extraction faster. The Toons above are capable of finding/providing the Items for you.
**You could also buy a {{II|Valve|name=false}} from the pre-game menu if you have at least 200 [[Ichor]].
*If you are {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, you could consider inviting some Toons that need to finish their Item Mastery as the Items you drop from doing Machines can help with those without losing {{Heart}}.
*If you are skilled enough, it is quite recommended to do a solo run, as you guarantee that you will be doing all the Machines on the Floor.

===Item Purchases from [[Dandy's Shop]]===
*Use [[Trinkets]] like {{TI|Fancy Purse|name=true}} and/or {{TI|Coin Purse|name=true}} to get {{Tape|name=true}} early on. Additionally, {{TI|Dandy Plush|name=true}} can also be used to give you a 50% discount on all Dandy's Shop Items, which is more beneficial than the previously mentioned Trinkets.
*Try to get [[Toons]] like  {{CI|Yatta|name=true}} and {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} who can generate [[Items]] for you, as using Items can give you more Tapes to buy from {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}. Note higher rarity Items give more Tapes upon use.
*Try using Extraction or Skill Check based Trinkets to extract [[Machines]] fast, as each Machine grants +10 Tapes upon fully completing it yourself.
*Voting on these [[Cards]] below can help with this Mastery quests:
**{{CDI|Blind Grab/Lost and Found|name=true}} will give everyone a random Item, which also gives some extra Tapes when you use them.
**{{CDI|Penny Pincher/Spare Change|name=false}} will give everyone an extra 45 Tapes.
**{{CDI|Frugal|name=false}} will give your whole team a 10% discount on Dandy's Shop Items.
**{{CDI|Avaricious/Covetous|name=false}} will make the rarer Items spawn more likely on the Floor, which will also give more Tapes when you use them. Keep in mind that this can also be a disadvantage as it also increases the rarity of Dandy's Shop Items, which can make them more costly to buy.

