==Trivia==
*On August 14, 2024, one of {{CI|Pebble|name=true}}'s Mastery requirements was changed from 'activate this [[Toon]]'s Passive [[Ability]] 30 times' to 'encounter 80 [[Twisteds]].' Those who had mastered Pebble still retained access to his Vintage Skin, but the sparkles disappeared from his icon until he was fully re-mastered.
**Before the update, Pebble and {{CI|Poppy|name=true}} were the only Toons requiring Passive Abilities to be used for Mastery requirements.
*[[Pebble]], {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}, and {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}'s Mastery requirements of reaching [[Floor]] 20 is widely considered to be the hardest Mastery requirement in the game. 
**Pebble, Bobette, Bassie, {{CI|Flutter|name=true}}, and {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] whose requirements necessitate reaching a certain Floor, the latter two requiring Floor 12.
**{{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} is the only [[Event]] {{Type|Main}} to not have a Mastery requirement of reaching Floor 20, and Pebble is the only base-game Main Character that requires you to reach Floor 20.
*{{CI|Goob|name=true}}, {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, {{CI|Coal|name=true}}, {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, [[Flyte]], {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}, [[Gourdy]], {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}, and {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] that require you to have another Toon with them for a certain amount of [[Floors]]. {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} is needed for Goob, {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} is needed for Sprout, [[Pebble]] is needed for Coal, {{CI|Looey|name=true}} is needed for Yatta, Flutter is needed for Flyte, Yatta is needed for Cocoa, both Yatta and Looey are needed for Blot, {{CI|Tisha|name=true}} is needed for Brusha, any [[Main Character]] is needed for [[Gourdy]], {{CI|Connie|name=true}} is needed for Soulvester, and {{CI|Brightney|name=true}} is needed for Squirm.
**Blot, Goob and Sprout require Mastery on the latter to be obtained while Coal, Yatta, Flyte, Cocoa, Brusha and Soulvester do not.
**Blot's Mastery quest of having Yatta and Looey survive a certain amount of Floors with him is the only occurrence of a Toon requiring 2 Toons present for this type of Mastery.
***Additionally, they must both be present for the Mastery quest to progress.
*[[Brusha]], {{CI|Eggson|name=true}}, [[Flyte]], [[Gourdy]], [[Looey]], [[Pebble]], {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, [[Sprout]], [[Tisha]], and  {{CI|Vee|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] that don't require the usage of [[Items]]. 
**However, all of these Toons do still require you to pick up Items.
**{{CI|Astro|name=true}} is the only base [[Main Character]] that does require Item usage.
**[[Gourdy]] is the only event Main Character that doesn't require Item usage for his Mastery.
*The [[Skins]] that are obtained from these quests were the only original Skins, before the introduction of Skins available in [[Dandy's Store]] (later [[Dyle's Store]]).
*Many [[Toons]] require Mastery on another Toon to unlock.
**[[Shelly]] requires 100% Mastery on [[Tisha]].
**[[Pebble]] requires 100% Mastery on {{CI|Toodles|name=true}}.
**[[Sprout]] requires 100% Mastery on [[Cosmo]].
**[[Vee]] requires 100% Mastery on [[Brightney]].
**[[Goob]] requires 50% Mastery on [[Scraps]].
**{{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} requires 50% Mastery on Goob.
***Waxwell and Goob are the only Toons to need 50% Mastery for a Toon, compared to the usual 100%.
**[[Looey]] requires 100% Mastery on [[Poppy]].
**[[Blot]] requires 100% Mastery on both [[Looey]] and [[Yatta]].
*[[Astro]] is the first Main Character [[Toon]] that doesn't require Mastery on another Toon, instead he requires an encounter with {{CI|Twisted Dandy|name=true}}.
**Additionally, none of the [[Event Main Characters]] require Mastery on another Toon. Instead, they require 3000 of their respective Event Currency.
*[[Pebble]], {{CI|Rodger|name=true}}, [[Vee]], {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}, [[Scraps]] and {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] with Masteries that require you to encounter a certain amount of [[Twisteds]].
*[[Looey]], [[Blot]], [[Waxwell]], and [[Goob]] are the only non-Main Character [[Toons]] that require Mastery on another Toon(s) to unlock.
*Mastery can currently be checked on a TV in the [[Elevator]] and opening your STATS button.
*{{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}} has one of the more annoying Masteries, as his abysmal Extraction Speed makes completing the required 30 [[Machines]] extremely slow. He also has to travel a lot of meters, something his 1{{Star}} Movement Speed and Stamina makes tedious.
**Completing Machines can be made much easier by equipping [[Vee's Remote]] or having someone prime all the Machines and letting you finish them.
**Not to mention, other [[Toons]] need to walk the same or even less with more Movement Speed, like [[Poppy]] or [[Yatta]].
*[[Cocoa]] is the first [[Toon]] to have a Mastery requirement to use a specific Item, that being {{II|BonBon|name=true}}; the second is [[Waxwell]], who needs {{II|Instructions|name=false}}.
**Cocoa is also the only Toon to not need her Active Ability to finish her Mastery, despite having one.
***One could argue that the Ability is the only way to get the BonBons, but it can be obtained from either another Cocoa or the {{CDI|Blind Grab/Lost and Found|name=true}} Cards.
*[[Blot]] is the first and currently only [[Toon]] who requires Mastery on two different Toons to be obtained, that being [[Looey]] and [[Yatta]].
**Additionally, he is also the first and currently only Toon to require two Toons present in a run for a Mastery Quest, also being Looey and Yatta.
*Every [[Toon]] requires traveling a certain amount of meters for their Mastery.
**[[Brusha]] needs to travel the least, with 40,000 meters, [[Blot]] needs the most as a non-[[Main Character]] with 120,000, and [[Pebble]] needs the most at 175,000.
***Pebble and [[Bassie]] are the only Main Character Toons to need to move more than 150,000 meters, with Bassie needing 160,000.
****The amount of meters a Toon needs to travel in a Mastery is extremely unbalanced and tedious to complete due to various hindrances.
*****Brusha, for example, who has 3 Star in [[Movement Speed]], only needs 40,000 meters, as stated above.
*****[[Yatta]], in spite of her high mobility, actually has the second-least meters to travel, being behind Brusha at 45,000 meters. Some would argue that this is quite unbalanced compared to Toons who have worse mobility compared to Yatta and have to travel more meters, like {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}, or Toons with similar mobility stats traveling a lot more meters, like [[Tisha]]. Yatta's Passive Ability being able to drop Box o' Chocolates or Speed Candies gives her even more of an unfair advantage.
*{{CI|Dandy|name=true}} and {{CI|Dyle|name=true}} are the only Toons to not have Mastery Quests as they are only accessible by developers. However, they could still get [[Toon of the Week]] Quests if they have one.
*Coincidentally, back when [[Brusha]] still had her Toggle [[Ability]], her Mastery tracked the Ability as "Active". This was indirectly fixed after her Ability rework in [[Changelog|v0.26.1]], turning it to an actual Active Ability.

